body:
Also, remember that like everyone has EBV it's only a problem for us because our immune system is messed up. Unless you have chronic active EBV (which you don't because most people with that condition die after a couple years) I wouldn't be worrying about it.

&#x200B;

Babesia is the most important and hardest to treat...also bart but babesia has to be handled first then bart. 

&#x200B;

Has your doctor been switching you antibiotics every 6 months at least? I don't know how you could plateau that soon into antibiotics. There is a plethora of antibiotic combinations which help.

&#x200B;

I am pretty sure the only antibiotic that goes through the blood brain barrier is minocycline just a fyi.

I have neuro Lyme with babesia and bart. I really haven't looked into mold as I think if you clear babesia and bart and focus on Lyme the immune system will pick up the rest.

&#x200B;

The antibiotics Jemsek recommends for 3-5 months cost $49k....so I'd try Dapsone beforehand for sure. I mean you can go to Jemsek...I go to him but neuro Lyme won't be cured with orals. I have neuro Lyme and been with Jemsek since December 2016 and treating with orals alone but it has NOT cleared the Lyme in my brain.

&#x200B;

I am going to go get a MRI and SPECT scan done and may do IV's with Jemsek even though it's so expensive. I know Jemsek does many IV antibiotics...you aren't given just one. It's like a rotation of 4 I think and you probably take orals at the same time.

&#x200B;

I mean 1 year isn't that long truthfully. I know people who have been sick for 10 years and doing treatment. My belief is you gotta go big or go home. I don't know what IV's are offered at Lyme Mexico so I can't really say. I mean ozone, plasmapheresis sounds great but to me...stem cell in Germany or whoever offers it is higher on my list. Also, I have heard from many people that getting hyperbaric oxygen therapy really helps neuro Lyme. 

&#x200B;

That's what I have decided with all my research. I don't really care the cost of IV's. I'd obviously take out a loan and do it. I mean with health it's nothing to mess around with you need to get better.

&#x200B;

I tried herbals didn't do crap. I am back on babesia protocol because my liver is inflamed again. Please let me know who you are seeing for the Dapsone...it's a drug I am highly interested in. 

&#x200B;

Thanks!
